{"id":"93a99642b1c854e4","group":"58","path":"58/batch13/58-df-self-adjoint-extension.md","title":"Self-Adjoint Extension","display":"df-self-adjoint-extension — Self-Adjoint Extension","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-self-adjoint-extension","aliases":["58-df-self-adjoint-extension","Self-Adjoint Extension"],"display":"df-self-adjoint-extension — Self-Adjoint Extension","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md]]","[[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-self-adjoint-extension"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-self-adjoint-extension</span><span>Self-Adjoint Extension</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-self-adjoint-extension — Self-Adjoint Extension"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"10205c9c4c85a35d\" href=\"?note=10205c9c4c85a35d\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md\">../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5998e080b5d378a0\" href=\"?note=5998e080b5d378a0\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md\">../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,T_U,H\\in V\">\\(T,T_U,H\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H\">\\(\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H\\)</span> (symmetric-operator predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"10205c9c4c85a35d\" href=\"?note=10205c9c4c85a35d\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md\">../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\)</span> (bounded self-adjoint-operator predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5998e080b5d378a0\" href=\"?note=5998e080b5d378a0\" title=\"../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md\">../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{SelfAdjointExtension}_S\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{SelfAdjointExtension}_S\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (self-adjoint-extension predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{SelfAdjointExtension}_S(T_U,T,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H(T)\\land T\\subseteq T_U\\land\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T_U,H)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{SelfAdjointExtension}_S(T_U,T,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H(T)\\land T\\subseteq T_U\\land\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T_U,H)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom now defines a bounded self-adjoint extension, the strongest notion supported by the available upstream adjoint predicate.  A general unbounded self-adjoint extension additionally requires an unbounded-adjoint graph/domain predicate.</li>\n<li>Self-adjoint: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T = T^*\">\\(T = T^*\\)</span>; spectrum real; unitary groups <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"e^{itT}\">\\(e^{itT}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Von Neumann: symmetric extensions correspond to unitary maps between deficiency spaces</li>\n<li>The condition <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n_+(T)=n_-(T)\">\\(n_+(T)=n_-(T)\\)</span> characterizes existence of self-adjoint extensions; the Cayley transform is related, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"1c3aae4ca0d902b6\" href=\"?note=1c3aae4ca0d902b6\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-cayley-transform.md\">../batch09/58-df-cayley-transform.md</a>.</li>\n<li>Essential self-adjoint: closure <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar{T}\">\\(\\bar{T}\\)</span> self-adjoint; unique self-adjoint extension</li>\n<li>Friedrichs: extension minimizing quadratic form; distinguished self-adjoint extension</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Titchmarsh, Eigenfunction Expansions</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"10205c9c4c85a35d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"5998e080b5d378a0","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md","status":"resolved","id":"10205c9c4c85a35d","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H$ (symmetric-operator predicate, see [[../batch12/58-df-symmetric-operator.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"5998e080b5d378a0","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S$ (bounded self-adjoint-operator predicate, see [[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-cayley-transform.md","status":"resolved","id":"1c3aae4ca0d902b6","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"The condition $n_+(T)=n_-(T)$ characterizes existence of self-adjoint extensions; the Cayley transform is related, see [[../batch09/58-df-cayley-transform.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,T_U,H\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{SelfAdjointExtension}_S\\subseteq V^3","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}extension} \\vdash \\mathrm{SelfAdjointExtension}_S(T_U,T,H)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Symmetric}_H(T)\\land T\\subseteq T_U\\land\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T_U,H)","display":true},{"tex":"T = T^*","display":false},{"tex":"e^{itT}","display":false},{"tex":"n_+(T)=n_-(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar{T}","display":false}],"bytes":1842,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1125","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-self-adjoint-extension.md|58-df-self-adjoint-extension]]（batch13）"}],"outgoing":["10205c9c4c85a35d","5998e080b5d378a0","1c3aae4ca0d902b6"]}